This solution uses a helper function `is_eligible` that checks whether a new queen can be placed at the given position. The `dfs` function then uses this helper function to recursively try all possible placements of queens. The total number of solutions is the return value of `dfs`. 

This solution has a time complexity of O(2^n), which is the worst-case time complexity for this problem. 

Note: This solution assumes that the queens are distinct and can't be placed in the same position. If this is not the case, the solution needs to be adjusted accordingly. 

